# Hubstr Relay — Caddy reverse proxy
# Automatic TLS + WebSocket upgrade + NIP-86 JSON-RPC
#
# Caddy implements RFC 8441 and RFC 9220, so WebSockets work over
# HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 with no special handling.
#
# TLS / certificates are fully automatic:
#   - On first start Caddy obtains a certificate from Let's Encrypt via ACME
#     (ZeroSSL is tried as a fallback) and renews it ~30 days before expiry.
#   - Ports 80 and 443 must be reachable from the internet for the ACME
#     challenge; port 80 is also where HTTP -> HTTPS redirection is served.
#   - Certificates and ACME account keys are stored under Caddy's data dir
#     (e.g. /var/lib/caddy/.local/share/caddy), not in /etc/letsencrypt.
# No certbot, no manual renewal, no redirect block required.

{
	# ACME account email — used for expiry notices. Replace with your own.
	email admin@example.com
}

# Replace with your own domain, e.g. relay.innis.xyz
relay.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080

	request_body {
		max_size 1MB
	}
}
